content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Sales Consultant",
      "description": "Employee who guides customers through selecting and evaluating vehicles"
    },
    {
      "name": "Vehicle",
      "description": "Car available for viewing, test driving, or purchase"
    },
    {
      "name": "Test Drive",
      "description": "Customer trial of a vehicle before deciding on a purchase"
    },
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "description": "Person interested in browsing, evaluating, or purchasing a vehicle"
    },
    {
      "name": "Feedback",
      "description": "Customer impressions about a vehicle or test drive"
    },
    {
      "name": "Finance Officer",
      "description": "Staff member who reviews financing eligibility and prepares agreements"
    },
    {
      "name": "Credit Application",
      "description": "Customer submission used to evaluate financing options"
    },
    {
      "name": "Car Purchase",
      "description": "Transaction record for buying a vehicle including financing details"
    },
    {
      "name": "Financing Option",
      "description": "Proposed loan terms available to a customer"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lease Agreement",
      "description": "Contract outlining terms for leasing a vehicle"
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory Manager",
      "description": "Employee who tracks vehicle availability and manages stock levels"
    },
    {
      "name": "Manufacturing Order",
      "description": "Order request for new vehicles sent to a manufacturer"
    },
    {
      "name": "Manufacturer",
      "description": "External vehicle producer receiving inventory orders"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Inventory Keeping": {
      "objects": [
        "Inventory Manager",
        "Vehicle",
        "Manufacturing Order",
        "Manufacturer"
      ]
    },
    "Consulting": {
      "objects": [
        "Sales Consultant",
        "Customer",
        "Vehicle",
        "Test Drive",
        "Feedback"
      ]
    },
    "Finances": {
      "objects": [
        "Customer",
        "Finance Officer",
        "Car Purchase",
        "Financing Option",
        "Lease Agreement",
        "Credit Application"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- In case an object appears in multiple bounded contexts, suggest a name change.
- Also suggest a name change if the meaning of the object is too similar to an object from another bounded context
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Inventory Keeping": {
      "derived from": "Inventory Keeping Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Inventory Manager",
        "Vehicle Record",
        "Manufacturing Order",
        "Manufacturer"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Vehicle -> Vehicle Record"
      ]
    },
    "Consulting": {
      "derived from": "Consulting Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Sales Consultant",
        "Customer",
        "Vehicle",
        "Test Drive",
        "Feedback"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Finances": {
      "derived from": "Finances Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Buyer",
        "Finance Officer",
        "Car Purchase",
        "Financing Option",
        "Lease Agreement",
        "Credit Application"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Customer -> Buyer"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
